Done. `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean for every file I touched (remaining errors are all yours: `lib/actions-hosting-sites.ts`, `app/api/hosting/thumb/route.ts`, `worker/hosting.ts`).

## Exact signatures

```ts
// lib/files-types.ts
export type FileMut = { ok: true } | { ok: false; error: string };
export type FileApi = {
  key: string;                 // "server:<id>" | "hosting:<accountId>:<root>"  — remount key
  rootLabel: string;           // "root" | "public_html" | "home" | …
  list(path: string): Promise<{ ok: true; entries: FileEntry[] } | { ok: false; error: string }>;
  read(path: string): Promise<{ ok: true; content: string } | { ok: false; error: string }>;
  save(path: string, content: string): Promise<FileMut>;
  mkdir(dir: string, name: string): Promise<FileMut>;
  rename(path: string, newName: string): Promise<FileMut>;
  remove(path: string, isDirectory: boolean): Promise<FileMut>;
  uploadUrl(dir: string): string;
  downloadUrl?(path: string): string | null;
  chmod?(path: string, mode: string): Promise<FileMut>;
};

// lib/files-adapters.ts  (plain module, no directive — client-safe)
export function serverFileApi(serverId: string): FileApi;      // has downloadUrl + chmod
export function hostingFileApi(accountId: string, root: string): FileApi; // has downloadUrl, NO chmod

// components/customer/files/FileBrowser.tsx  ("use client")
export function FileBrowser({ api, initialPath = "/" }: { api: FileApi; initialPath?: string });
export function ServerFileBrowser({ serverId, initialPath }: { serverId: string; initialPath?: string });

// components/customer/files/UploadQueue.tsx
export function useUploadQueue(api: FileApi, path: string, onDone: () => void);
// → { items, enqueue, cancel, dismiss, clearDone, busy }  (unchanged)
```

Pass the adapter memoized (`useMemo`) and use `key={api.key}` on `<FileBrowser>` when the source can change.

## File by file

- **lib/files-types.ts** — added `FileMut` + `FileApi` exactly as specced, with a comment explaining the two-backend reason. `FileEntry` untouched.
- **lib/files-adapters.ts** (new) — `serverFileApi` wraps the existing `lib/actions-files` actions 1:1 (unwraps `listFiles`'s extra `path` and `readFile`'s `path`/`truncated`; `remove` ignores `isDirectory` since `deleteEntry(serverId, path)` stats it itself). `hostingFileApi` maps `"/"→root`, `"/a/b"→"<root>/a/b"`.
- **lib/actions-hosting-fs.ts** (new, `"use server"`) — `hostingFsList/Read/Save/Mkdir/Rename/Delete`. Owner-or-admin + `status === "ACTIVE"` replicated from `ownedAccountWithNode`. SANDBOX: list → `{ ok:true, entries: [] }` (no invented files), read → the "no hosting node is attached" message, mutations → `{ ok:true }`. Read caps at 1 MB via `fsStatSize` before buffering; save caps too.
- **lib/hosting-fs.ts** — added `fsRename(t, fromRel, toRel)` (`withSftp` + `safeRel` on both ends); `FsEntry` gained `mode: number | null` and `fsList` now plumbs the real `attrs.mode` through (it was already reading it to derive `isDir`), converted to an octal string in the action. No fabricated `"644"`.
- **app/api/hosting/files/route.ts** — added a `relOr400` helper applying `safeRel` up front on both GET and POST, returning 400 on a bad path. Confinement was already there transitively (every `hosting-fs` primitive calls `safeRel`); this makes arbitrary nested paths explicit and turns a bad path into a clear 400 instead of a 500/404. `MAX_UPLOAD`/`MAX_DOWNLOAD`/`ownedNode` untouched.
- **components/customer/files/UploadQueue.tsx** — only the destination changed: `api.uploadUrl(path)` in `xhr.open`, deps `[api.key, path, onDone]`. XHR byte progress, one-at-a-time, `beginUpload`/`endUpload` all untouched.
- **components/customer/files/FileBrowser.tsx** — all seven direct action calls replaced by `api.*`; `TreeNode` takes `api`; breadcrumb root and tree root use `api.rootLabel` (`"/ (root)"` still renders identically for VPS); row Download link now `api.downloadUrl?.(full) ?? null`. Bulk delete looks the row up in `entries` to pass `isDirectory`. Doc comment rewritten to explain the adapter indirection. Every feature, class and token preserved; the "DELIBERATELY ABSENT: move and copy" note kept and reworded to `rename`.
- **app/dashboard/servers/[id]/page.tsx** — import and both call sites → `<ServerFileBrowser serverId={server.id} />`. Nothing else changed.

## Server-component call site

I took the **thin client wrapper** route. `serverFileApi` returns an object of closures, which cannot cross the RSC boundary as a prop, so `ServerFileBrowser` (exported from FileBrowser.tsx, which is already `"use client"`) builds the adapter internally with `useMemo` and renders `<FileBrowser key={api.key} api={api} />`.

## Two things worth knowing

One gotcha I had to work around: `ownedAccountWithNode`'s `{ error } | { user, a }` union does **not** narrow under this tsconfig — `if ("error" in ctx)` leaves `ctx.error` as `string | undefined`, which is exactly the TS2322 you're seeing at `actions-hosting-sites.ts:458` and `:602`. I gave my copy an explicit `ok` discriminant; same fix applies to yours.

What the hosting backend genuinely **cannot** do, so the UI stays honest:
- **No chmod.** No primitive exists; `hostingFileApi` omits the property. (FileBrowser has never rendered a permissions control for either backend, so nothing needed gating — but the flag is there if you add one, and `serverFileApi` does supply `chmod`.)
- **No move/copy** on either backend — rename stays within one parent.
- **Delete is not recursive.** `fsDelete` uses SFTP `rmdir`, which only removes an empty directory, unlike the VPS's recursive `removePath`. I made the directory-delete failure message say so. If you want recursive folder delete for hosting, it needs a new primitive.
- **`safeRel` restricts path characters** to `[A-Za-z0-9._/\- ]`, so a file whose name contains anything else (unicode, `@`, `#`, `'`) is unreachable — it will list fine but reading, renaming, deleting or downloading it throws "invalid path chars".
- **No stat/`isDirectory` disambiguation server-side** — `hostingFsDelete` trusts the caller's `isDirectory`, which the browser takes from the listing.
- **`root: ""` maps to `"."`, not `""`** — one deviation from your spec, deliberate: `safeRel("")` returns `"public_html"`, so an empty mapped path would silently drop a home-rooted browser into the docroot. `"."` is the directory the chrooted session actually starts in.
